the domain, two intersection coordinates per pair, the required above/below
regions and nonnegative-parameter checks. 949 has both named pairs, their
unique intersection coordinates and branch rejection. The author explicitly
retains graphical construction in its production notes. Extra plotting tables
and the unasked inequality regions included in frozen 949 are not prerequisites
for this static comparison. No actual rendering was examined or approved.

954 includes each required square rewrite, not merely its final value.
952 retains every substitution in original order. Shared derivations in
943/944/952/953 are specific and correctly mapped; duplicating them per value
is unnecessary.

The current author retains logical 956, printed 936 and
`p0290-numbering-936-to-956`, matching frozen FIRST. No competing printed-936
exercise is read. Parameter domains, zero cases, open/closed endpoints and
undefined-real flags agree across all affected tasks. 958's overlapping
piecewise boundary cases are equivalent, not contradictory.

The parent finding binds the same frozen FIRST JSON byte hash and the same
preserved author filename, and still says REVISE. Current
`independent_review=false` and working status are not misread as approval.

Only `compare-FIRST/review.md` and `compare-FIRST/review.json` were created.
FIRST, author files and the finding were left unchanged. There were zero new
source solves, source/definition reads, images, validators, tests, browser/DB/Git
